## Why This Is Asked
Tests secure, rotating certs in Swarm with Vault, handling cert storage (secret vs volume), and canary semantics.

## Key Concepts
- Swarm multi-node with TLS and mTLS
- Vault PKI for dynamic certs
- Certs via writable volume + sidecar refresh
- Canary rollout with health checks and rollback
- Nginx TLS termination and service-to-service mTLS

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple cert refresh watcher from Vault to a mounted volume
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
const fs = require('fs');
async function refresh() {
  const res = await fetch('https://vault.example/v1/pki/issue/api', { headers: { 'X-Vault-Token': process.env.VAULT_TOKEN } });
  const cert = await res.text();
  fs.writeFileSync('/certs/api.crt', cert);
}
setInterval(refresh, 5 * 60 * 1000);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate cert rotation does not break existing connections?
- How would you monitor Vault token renewal and automatic revocation?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design a tenant-scoped edge cache, ensure cross-DC coherence, and integrate with a docker-dca workflow including bootstrap commands and compose scaffolding.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant caching with tenant-scoped cache keys
- TTLs sourced from a central config service
- Cache invalidation on mutating requests and cross-DC coherence
- Edge proxy placement with TLS termination and header-based tenanting
- Observability and basic failure handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Skeleton: per-tenant cache with TTL and invalidation broadcast
class TenantCache {
  constructor(configServiceUrl, pubSub) {
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.configServiceUrl = configServiceUrl;
    this.pubSub = pubSub;

    this.pubSub.subscribe('invalidate', (tenantId, path) => {
      this.invalidate(tenantId, path);
    });
  }

  async get(tenantId, path) {
    const ttl = await this.getTTL(tenantId);
    const key = `${tenantId}:${path}`;
    const entry = this.cache.get(key);

    if (entry && Date.now() < entry.expiresAt) {
      return entry.value;
    }
    return null;
  }

  async set(tenantId, path, value) {
    const ttl = await this.getTTL(tenantId);
    const key = `${tenantId}:${path}`;
    this.cache.set(key, {
      value,
      expiresAt: Date.now() + ttl
    });
  }

  async invalidate(tenantId, path) {
    const key = `${tenantId}:${path}`;
    this.cache.delete(key);
  }

  async broadcastInvalidation(tenantId, path) {
    await this.pubSub.publish('invalidate', tenantId, path);
  }

  async getTTL(tenantId) {
    // Fetch from central config service
    const config = await fetch(`${this.configServiceUrl}/tenants/${tenantId}`);
    return config.cacheTTL || 300;
  }
}
```

## Bootstrap Commands

```bash
# Build the sidecar image
docker build -t edge-cache-sidecar ./sidecar

# Deploy to docker-dca cluster
docker-dca deploy --file docker-compose.yml --service edge-cache-sidecar
```

## Docker Compose Skeleton

```yaml
version: '3.8'
services:
  api:
    image: your-api:latest
    ports:
      - "8080:8080"

  edge-cache:
    image: edge-cache-sidecar:latest
    ports:
      - "8081:8081"
    environment:
      - CONFIG_SERVICE_URL=http://config-service:8080
      - PUB_SUB_URL=redis://redis:6379
    depends_on:
      - api
      - redis

  nginx:
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
      - "443:443"
    volumes:
      - ./nginx.conf:/etc/nginx/nginx.conf:ro
    depends_on:
      - edge-cache

  redis:
    image: redis:7-alpine

  config-service:
    image: config-service:latest
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests depth of cross-DC security, dynamic policy loading, and automated risk controls in a real-world Docker DC architecture.

## Key Concepts

- SPIFFE/SVIDs with Vault
- WASM-based per-tenant policy engine
- Edge verifier sidecar for SVID validation
- Canary deployments and automatic rollback
- Cross-DC routing and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: load tenant policy from broker and validate SVID before calling app
async function handleRequest(req){
  const svid = await verifySVID(req.headers['spiffe']);
  const(policy) = await loadPolicyFromBroker(req.tenant);
  if(!policy.allows(req)) throw new Error('Access denied');
  return proxyToApp(req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you debug a scenario where Vault rotation invalidates existing SVIDs mid-rollout?
- What metrics and traces would you collect to enforce the 25% canary SLA thresholds across DCs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant QoS with dynamic config in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik RateLimit middleware, Redis store, per-tenant quotas, Docker Config
- TLS termination, hot-reload without restart, cross-DC coordination
- Request tagging with X-Tenant and validation of isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo middleware sketch: extract tenant and enforce quota from Redis
async function enforceTenantRate(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const quota = await redisGetQuota(tenant);
  if (quota.allow(req)) return next();
  res.status(429).send('Too Many Requests');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit cross-DC quota drift and recover from Redis replication lag?
- How would you test hot-reload behavior under config churn?

